# Pawple — Global safe area, spacing & composition

Apply consistently across **all** current and future Pawple screens. Map numbers to `theme.js` where possible; when theme lacks a token, prefer extending the theme over one-off magic numbers.

## Core philosophy

Screens must **never** feel: packed, dense, form-heavy, maximized for content, mechanically spaced, or edge-to-edge crowded.

Screens **should** feel: airy, balanced, intentionally composed, calmly suspended, easy to breathe through. **Whitespace is part of the design language.**

- **Do not** optimize for “fitting more on screen.”
- **Do** optimize for “making interaction feel effortless.”
- **When unsure:** remove rather than add. Prefer clarity over completeness, calmness over density, emotion over functionality. The interface should feel inevitable, not designed.

**Product feel:** “Nothing extra exists.” Users feel emotionally relaxed, visually calm, gently guided — not cognitively loaded or operationally overwhelmed.

## Safe areas (devices)

Always respect: Dynamic Island, camera cutouts, punch holes, gesture bars, rounded corners, home indicators.

**Never:** headers hugging the top edge, CTAs cramped on the gesture area, content colliding with hardware.

Use `SafeAreaView` / safe-area context and tab-bar height where relevant; verify on notched and gesture-nav devices.

## Top spacing (after safe-area inset)

| Target | Value |
|--------|--------|
| **Minimum** top spacing below safe area | **32px** |
| **Ideal** | **36–40px** |

The first prominent element (usually the page title) must **not** feel visually attached to the status bar, notch, punch hole, or top edge. Top should feel calm, premium, breathable — not compressed or “cramped-app.”

## Bottom spacing

Bottom CTAs and nav must **not** feel cramped against gesture bar, home indicator, keyboard, or raw screen edge.

| Target | Value |
|--------|--------|
| **Minimum** bottom padding (above system UI) | **24–34px** |

Sticky CTA strips: float slightly above the bottom edge; calm and intentional; add soft top separation (hairline, subtle fill, or spacing) when needed.

## Horizontal page padding

| Context | Value |
|---------|--------|
| **Default** horizontal padding | **24px** |
| **Large composition sections** | **28px** (optional) |

**Avoid:** defaulting everything to 16px-wide gutters, overly narrow margins, crowded horizontal composition.

## Vertical rhythm (non-uniform)

Avoid equal spacing top-to-bottom. Use **tiered** rhythm so layout feels guided and relaxed, not mechanical.

| Tier | Range | Use for |
|------|--------|---------|
| **Micro** | 4–8px | Icon ↔ text, tight label hints |
| **Small** | 10–14px | Label → field |
| **Medium** | 20–28px | Related grouped sections |
| **Large** | 32–40px | Major section separation |
| **XL breathing** | 48–64px | Emotional reset / hero areas |

**Do not** use mathematically identical gaps for every block on a screen.

## Forms & inputs

Forms must **not** feel enterprise, dashboard-like, or mechanically stacked.

| Property | Guideline |
|----------|-----------|
| Input height | **56–58px** |
| Input radius | **16–18px** |
| Tone | Lightweight, conversational, emotionally soft |

**Avoid:** dense forms, tiny spacing, excessive labels, helper-text overload.

## Cards

| Property | Guideline |
|----------|-----------|
| Radius | **18–24px** |
| Inner padding | **18–22px** |
| Vertical spacing between cards | **10–16px** |

Cards should feel floating, soft, breathable.

**Avoid:** heavy borders, aggressive shadows, compressed card content.

## Typography

Type should breathe.

**Avoid:** stacked dense text, tiny metadata overload, excessive font-weight jumps.

- Page titles: strong breathing room **above**, generous spacing **below**.
- Metadata: subtle, secondary, visually quiet.

## Primary buttons

| Property | Guideline |
|----------|-----------|
| Height | **48–52px** |
| Radius | **999px** (full pill) |

Primary CTAs should feel calm, stable, touchable, emotionally soft.

**Avoid:** buttons touching screen edges, crowding content, aggressive visual weight.

## Scrolling

Scrolling should feel light, breathable, frictionless.

**Avoid:** too many competing focal elements at once, overwhelming vertical stacking, information density for density’s sake.

## Animation & motion

| Property | Guideline |
|----------|-----------|
| Duration | **180–280ms** |
| Easing | **ease-out**; soft spring only if needed |

Motion should feel subtle, soft, natural, emotionally invisible.

**Avoid:** aggressive movement, heavy spring, flashy transitions.

## Active-pet bottom-tab labels

Bottom-tab labels showing a pet name use Inter, consistent with `.cursorrules`
typography. Truncate names with an ellipsis beyond approximately 12 characters,
and fall back to the static label when no active pet exists.

## Implementation note

Prefer **theme tokens** and **semantic names** (e.g. `screenPaddingHorizontal`, `sectionGapLarge`) when adding these values to `theme.js`, so screens stay aligned with this document as the single source of truth for composition intent.
